From 708b71467b5c1016cb86161727ed84da76875983 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mattephi <ialentev@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 20:49:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Newton backend: find CUDA 13 runtime, and fix
 keyword-only writer calls

Two upstream bugs in the Newton backend that block UWLab's OmniReset tasks.

1. newton_manager.py: the CUDA runtime probe only tries libcudart.so.12 and the
   unversioned libcudart.so. Isaac Sim 6.0 / torch cu130 ship CUDA 13, whose pip
   wheel installs libcudart.so.13 under site-packages/nvidia/cu13/lib with no
   unversioned symlink and that directory not on the loader path. Both attempts
   fail, so relaxed-mode graph capture is disabled and Newton silently falls back
   to EAGER execution -- surfacing only as a warning while costing a large part of
   its speed advantage. Now tries .13 first, then the older names, then locates
   the pip-installed runtime via sysconfig. Verified: the run now logs "Newton
   CUDA graph captured (deferred relaxed mode, RTX-compatible)".

2. rigid_object.py: write_root_{link,com}_{pose,velocity}_to_sim_index are all
   keyword-only (note the `*` in their signatures), but the deprecated
   write_root_state_to_sim / write_root_link_state_to_sim wrappers call them
   positionally, so every call raises
       TypeError: ... takes 1 positional argument but 2 were given
   Six sites fixed to pass by keyword. This is what broke the Near-Goal reset
   family, which replays object poses from the partial-assembly bank.

